{"id":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#thm:van-kampen-theorem","title":"thm:van-kampen-theorem","path":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.md","line":342,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex#thm:van-kampen-theorem","uses":["[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#prop:free-product-universal-property]]","[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1#lem:loop-decomposition-open-cover]]","[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:van-kampen-rectangular-subdivision]]","[[references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/formalization-support#lem:van-kampen-grid-cell-sweep]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Hatcher/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter1.tex","label":"thm:van-kampen-theorem","line":538,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[Van Kampen's theorem]\n\\label{thm:van-kampen-theorem}\n\\uses{prop:free-product-universal-property, lem:loop-decomposition-open-cover, lem:van-kampen-rectangular-subdivision, lem:van-kampen-grid-cell-sweep}\n\\dcref{ch1:1.20}\n\\group{Fundamental Group}\n\nLet $X=\\bigcup_\\alpha A_\\alpha$, where the $A_\\alpha$ are path-connected open\nsets containing $x_0$ and all pairwise intersections are path-connected. The\nmap $\\Phi:*_\\alpha\\pi_1(A_\\alpha)\\to\\pi_1(X)$ is surjective. If all triple\nintersections are path-connected, its kernel is the normal subgroup generated\nby $i_{\\alpha\\beta}(\\omega)i_{\\beta\\alpha}(\\omega)^{-1}$ for\n$\\omega\\in\\pi_1(A_\\alpha\\cap A_\\beta)$, and\n\\[\n\\pi_1(X)\\cong *_\\alpha\\pi_1(A_\\alpha)/N.\n\\]\n\\end{theorem}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[Van Kampen&#x27;s theorem] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a76616e2d6b616d70656e2d7468656f72656d\"></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2